             Robots="index, follow" />

<main class="legal-page">
    <article class="legal-document">
        <p class="legal-eyebrow">Legal &amp; Privacy</p>
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">Service information draft — operator identity and final legal terms need review before public launch.</p>

        <section>
            <h2>About the service</h2>
            <p>
                Comfidiario is an online journaling application operated by an individual based in Peru.
                The operator's full legal name and postal address have not yet been provided for this page.
                These terms describe the current service at a high level and should be reviewed and completed
                before the service is publicly launched.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Access and cost</h2>
            <p>
                The application is intended to be free to use. Donations are entirely optional and are not
                required to create, access, or use notebook features. Online donation processing is not
                currently enabled. The service may change as it is developed.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Your account and content</h2>
            <p>
                You are responsible for the accuracy of the account information you provide, keeping your
                sign-in credentials private, and activity performed through your account. Do not use the
                service to break the law, interfere with the service, or attempt to access another person's
                account or data.
            </p>
            <p>
                You retain responsibility for the content you enter and for keeping any separate copies you
                may need. Journal entries are personal data; the service's encryption and storage practices
                are described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. The application is not a
                substitute for secure independent backups.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
            <p>
                The service is provided online and may be unavailable, changed, or discontinued. No specific
                availability, backup restoration, or data recovery guarantee is stated here. The operator
                should complete and legally review these terms, including any consumer rights or mandatory
                protections that apply to a user's location.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Account closure</h2>
            <p>
                You can delete your account using the account deletion page. The application deletes the
                account and associated journals and entries from its active database. Backup, hosting, and
                diagnostic systems may retain copies under their own retention processes; those periods are
                not specified here.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
            <p>
                These terms may be updated as the service changes. A revision date and a process for notifying
                users of material changes should be established before public launch.
            </p>
        </section>

        <nav class="legal-page-links" aria-label="Other legal pages">
            <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
            <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>
